<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean export regs. 8.2 mln tns by June 30.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean export regs. 8.2 mln tns by June 30.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil registered 8.2 million tonnes of soybeans for export by June 30, according to government figures released by the Brazilian Association of Vegetable Oils Industries (Abiove).</p>
<p>Export registrations for soymeal totalled 8.5 million tonnes and for soyoil they were 822,000 tonnes, according to figures from the state export department Secex.</p>
<p>All figures refer to the 1997/98 marketing year (February-January).</p>
<p>For soymeal, the amount registered represented 95.6 percent of total forecast exports, up sharply from 72.2 percent at the same time last year.</p>
<p>The difference was even greater for soyoil, where 96.7 percent of projected exports had already been registered, compared with 69.5 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>The percentage for soybeans was only slightly higher than last year at 96.3 percent.</p>
<p>Following are total crop, crushing and export forecasts together with export registrations, in thousands of tonnes unless otherwise indicated:</p>
<p>					1997/98	    1996/97</p>
<p>Total crop			    26,400	     23,871</p>
<p>Crushing				18,000	     20,082</p>
<p>Exports</p>
<p>    - soybeans			8,500		3,633</p>
<p>    - soymeal			 8,900	     10,795</p>
<p>    - soyoil			    850		1,337</p>
<p>Export registrations</p>
<p>    - soybeans			8,188		3,338</p>
<p>    - soymeal			 8,512		7,797</p>
<p>    - soyoil			    822		  929</p>
<p>Registrations/exports (%)</p>
<p>    - soybeans			 96.3		 91.9</p>
<p>    - soymeal			  95.6		 72.2</p>
<p>    - soyoil			   96.7		 69.5</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo +55 11 248 5417))</p>
</text>
